<div class="mb-12 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-6" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 space-y-6">
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">Does the evidence show that AI works in healthcare?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">It shows that specific tools, tested in specific settings, produced specific results. A Swedish randomized trial of about 106,000 women reported fewer interval cancers with AI-supported mammography reading, and a randomized scribe trial reported a modest time saving for one of two tools. Neither result can be assumed for other tools or settings.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">Which AI uses have the strongest evidence?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">Among the studies summarized here, the two randomized trials are the strongest designs: the MASAI mammography trial and a UCLA randomized trial of ambient scribes. The sepsis alert evidence is largely reported by the developers, and the patient-communication guidance rests on design principles rather than outcome trials.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">What should a small clinic take from this?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">Start with administrative tasks, ask any supplier for independent evidence and error rates, keep a person responsible for every clinical decision, and run a small supervised pilot before widening scope.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">Is this medical or legal advice?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">No. It summarizes published evidence and its limits. Requirements differ by country and practice type, so confirm legal and regulatory duties with your own advisers.</p></div>
  </div>
</div>

